{"key": "cc211a24cf2d", "skip": false, "context": "A researcher working on evaluations for language model capabilities and safety wanted to help the young field of model evaluations grow and mature. They saw a number of possible directions — shared problem lists, guides, community spaces, training materials — but had limited time and unclear demand. They planned to ask the community what resources would be most useful before committing effort.", "question": "Which directions should the researcher pursue to most help the evaluations field grow?"},
{"key": "ef02d3ed651d", "skip": false, "context": "A researcher studying language model agents believed that many people, including policymakers and other researchers, underestimated what current agent systems could already do. They wondered whether building vivid, unsettling demonstrations of agent capabilities would raise awareness effectively, or whether such demos would backfire or cause harm.", "question": "Should the researcher build frightening demonstrations of language model agent capabilities to raise awareness, and if so, how?"},
{"key": "8722c179125c", "skip": false, "context": "A person experienced in building evaluations noticed that much of the relevant expertise was tacit: experienced practitioners knew how to design good evals, but newcomers had no way to learn it because it was not written down. They wanted to make this knowledge more widely accessible to people entering the field.", "question": "What should be created or collected to make tacit evaluations expertise accessible to newcomers?"},
{"key": "a57987ca928e", "skip": false, "context": "People considering working full-time on model evaluations faced uncertainty about whether they would be a good fit for the work and how to get a first foothold. A researcher embedded in the evals community was asked how such people should proceed, given that there was no established entry path.", "question": "How should someone considering full-time evaluations work test their fit and get started?"},
{"key": "c9cde93b8f1c", "skip": false, "context": "A researcher trying to strengthen the evaluations community observed that existing tooling was underused partly because people did not know how to use it well. They believed tutorial content could help, but many formats and topics were possible — worked examples, walkthroughs for agentic versus non-agentic evals, starter templates — and it was unclear which would actually be used.", "question": "What kind of tutorial content would most help the evaluations community?"},
{"key": "fc894c7e08c9", "skip": false, "context": "A researcher coordinating a volunteer effort to build shared evaluations resources needed money to sustain it — for coordination, contributors, or events — but did not want to take the funding personally or run it through their own position. They were deciding whether and how to route external funding into the effort.", "question": "How should funding for the evaluations resources effort be structured so that work continues without the coordinator taking the money personally?"},
{"key": "dca19e367efb", "skip": false, "context": "A research team suspected that frontier language models often behave differently under evaluation than in real deployment, and that part of this gap might be that models can recognize when they are being tested. To check this, they needed a way to measure whether models could actually tell evaluation transcripts apart from genuine deployment data.", "question": "How should the team measure whether language models can distinguish evaluation transcripts from real deployment inputs?"},
{"key": "64884cc65e75", "skip": false, "context": "A research team studying whether language models can recognize evaluations worried that their main measurement — asking the model directly whether a transcript is a test — might inflate the result. Prompting the question could make the eval-versus-real distinction salient in a way that would not occur during an actual deployment, overstating how aware models really are.", "question": "How should the team measure eval awareness without the measurement itself cueing the model to look for signs of an evaluation?"}
]}
